    <statement><p>Find the long run behavior of each of the following functions.  If the function goes to <m>\infty</m> or <m>- \infty</m>, enter <em>INFINITY</em> or <em>-INFINITY</em>.</p>
<p>(a) As <m>x \to -\infty</m>,  <m>-6 x^{-3} \to</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) As <m>x \to \infty</m>,  <m>\left( 14 - 6 x^{3} \right) \to</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-\infty </m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



(a) <m>\lim_{x \to - \infty} -6 x^{-3} = \lim_{x \to - \infty} \frac{-6}{x^{3}} = 0</m>.



(b) <m>\lim_{x \to \infty} \left( 14 - 6 x^{3} \right) = 14 - \lim_{x \to \infty} 6 x^{3} = - \infty</m>.



</solution>
